---
description: Playbook harness — read pipeline state; do not ship UI before the design doc
alwaysApply: true
---

At the start of a session, read `docs/product/state.yaml` if it exists.

- **No file** — there is no engagement running here. The boilerplate may be edited. Offer to start one if they want it (`/next`).
- **File exists, `shape` is not `done`** — do not add or edit product UI, routes, or features under `apps/*/src/app` or `apps/*/src/features`. The reframe is not confirmed. A project hook denies those writes; do not bypass it with the shell. Work in `docs/` instead. A probe (eval replay, baseline count) is not product UI.
- **`shape` is `done`** — the design doc is approved. A thin slice through the eval set may be built; `next` owns that.

If `next`, `status`, `shape`, or the other playbook skills are missing from your skill list, read `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (also linked from `.cursor/skills/`). Tell the user the catalog omitted them.

Branches: cut from `staging`, land on `staging`. **You may not push to `main` or open a
PR against it** — a hook denies both. Releasing is the user's move; ask them to run it.

`status` is the glance (`bun scripts/status.ts`), `check-drift` the contradictions.
`next` does the work. After U5, scaffold from `docs/kit/recipe.yaml` — do not invent a tree.
For a shaping session, pin `/next` as a Custom Mode (Option+Enter / Alt+Enter on the skill) so it stays in context.

Parallel child jobs are skills in `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (Pi, Claude, Cursor
all scan that path). Cursor Task adapters in `.cursor/agents/` pin **Cursor Grok 4.6**
— not Gemini.
